+# Skill: ORC and Orchestration Lab Session Coherence Guard
+
+Run at the end of a work session, before commit or handoff. Check only this session's change, in each repository it
+touched: ORC (`~/pro/orchestrator`, or the worktree used) and the lab (`~/scopes/scope-orchestration-lab`).
+
+## Where things live
+- Authorised intent: lab `scope.yaml`, `SCOPE.md`, `STATE.md` "North star" and `decisions/`; lab
+  `memory/authority-rules-step-1.md`; ORC `README.md` ("Direction", "Boundary") and `AGENTS.md`. Steward: Justin.
+- Current state and next steps: lab `STATE.md`. Read it first. ORC has no state file of its own.
+- Decisions: lab `decisions/` for this Scope. For ORC: open, pending Justin's answer on where ORC's decisions live.
+  A choice about one issue goes on that issue, under orchestrator#140.
+- Rules owned elsewhere: `~/pro/local-config/home/AGENTS.md`; ORC `SECURITY-REVIEW.md` and `dangerfile.js`;
+  orchestrator#140's description; `~/pro/agentic/HOW_NOT_TO_PLAN.md`, through lab `AGENTS.md` "Pace".
+
+## What changed this session
+Run in each repository the session touched:
+```bash
+git log --oneline "$START"..HEAD          # commits
+git diff "$START" HEAD                    # what they changed
+git status --short
+git diff --cached                         # staged: what the next commit holds
+git diff                                  # unstaged
+git ls-files --others --exclude-standard  # untracked: read those that matter
+```
+Add live changes, each with the time it was read: `pnpm service:status` (the build ORC runs), `pnpm list:approval-grants`,
+`pnpm status:agent-packages`, and every card this session raised or approved.
+If the start point is unknown, compare against `origin/main` and report "coverage incomplete".
+
+## Intent
+Does this change fit the authorised intent above? If not:
+
+> When this session's work and the authorised intent disagree:
+>
+> 1. Decide which it is: a defect in the work, an adaptation within what is already authorised, or a change of
+>    intent nobody has decided.
+> 2. Fix a defect in the work.
+> 3. Go ahead with an adaptation within existing authorisation, and record its reason where that helps. Record an
+>    undecided change of intent as a proposal for Justin in the decision record named under "Where things live",
+>    marked as awaiting him; work that depends on it waits for the decision.
+> 4. Do not edit lab `scope.yaml`, `SCOPE.md` or `STATE.md` "North star", or ORC `README.md` "Direction" and
+>    "Boundary" or `AGENTS.md`, to match the work unless Justin has recorded that decision.
+> 5. Correct a document directly only when a recorded decision of Justin's already settles it, and cite that decision.
+> 6. Before making a description, an implementation and a check agree, establish which of them is wrong. A test or
+>    the code shows what is checked or built; it does not authorise weakening a documented constraint.
+
+(Intent-change rule v2, from entropy-guard.)
+
+## Checks
+- If ORC's `src/`, `config/` or `test/architecture.test.ts` changed what a model, subprocess or network call can reach:
+  do `AGENTS.md` "Boundaries" and `README.md` "Boundary" still describe it, and does the test still assert it?
+- If an `ORCHESTRATOR_*` environment variable, a `package.json` script or a credential read changed: do `README.md`
+  "Run" and "Credentials" name only what the code reads?
+- If a path that grants, approves or activates authority, or reads credentials, was changed or added: is it in
+  `GUARDED` in `dangerfile.js`, and does the pull request carry a `## Security review` section?
+- If this session ran a `pnpm grant:*`, `revoke:*` or `request:approval-grant` command, approved a card, or edited
+  `config/installation.ts`: report each authority change, who approved it, and where it is recorded.
+- If ORC changed what a Scope package consumes (`src/package-api.ts`, a task-type declaration, a card template): name
+  each package affected, and whether it was rebuilt and its build card approved.
+- If this session opened issues or marked work on the map: does `node tools/map.mjs --check` pass, and are this
+  session's marks cleared with `node tools/map.mjs stopped`?
+- For each claim changed in `STATE.md`: do its other mentions agree, does each live fact say where and when it was read,
+  and does the file hold current state only, within its line cap? (Open: lab `AGENTS.md` and `STATE.md` state
+  different caps.)
+- If Justin decided something this session: is it in its decision record, dated and attributed, before `STATE.md`
+  links to it?
+- If something broke in real use: is it in `FRICTION.md`, newest first, marked (workshop) where only the workshop has
+  it? Is an ORC fact in ORC, a relationship fact in lab `memory/`, a new agent or tool idea committed in `AGENT_IDEAS.md`?
+- If this session added a markdown file at ORC's root: is it a description of current behaviour, or a session or
+  branch report that belongs in lab `reports/` or carries a "Historical" banner?
+- When two documents describe one thing, decide which owns it and reduce the other to a link. Keep summaries and
+  independent tests of the same contract.
+```bash
+# ORC: CI runs only Danger, so tests run here until orchestrator#144 lands
+pnpm typecheck && pnpm test
+pnpm test:e2e                                   # when web/ or src/adapters/browser/ changed
+grep -rhoE "\bORCHESTRATOR_[A-Z_]+" src config scripts | sort -u   # compare with README.md
+# lab
+node tools/map.mjs --check
+# both, only if `command -v lychee` finds it: links in the markdown this session changed
+lychee --offline <changed .md files>
+```
